<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tirant lo Blanc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1490</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tirant lo Blanc is a chivalric romance in Catalan by the Valencian knight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joanot-martorell">Joanot Martorell</a>, completed after his death by Martí Joan de Galba and printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in 1490. Realistic and humorous, it tells of a knight who saves the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, and it was praised by Cervantes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-quixote">Don Quixote</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tirant-lo-blanc.jpg" alt="Tirant lo Blanc" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tirante_el_Blanco_1511.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
